  "novel_mechanics_found": "Level 5 splits shape construction across two distinct objects. The upper black glyph cycles base shapes; its second state is [110,011,101]. The previously unexplained lower black/blue sprite is an orientation transformer: from the west-side approach at player cell x14,y35, the contact sequence right,right,left (443) transformed that base into the exact required [101,110,011] target. The color pinwheel still cycles C->9->E->8, but L5 starts with only 21 counter actions and each verified green-center ring resets the counter to 21. The upper-left and lower-left rings were both collected live.",
  "narrative": "The resolver supplied a 244-action prefix, and I replayed it from a fresh reset twice; both replays reached frame.levels_completed=4. I then explored L5 strictly from frames and actions. A compact attempt reached the lower-left ring with the exact required target shape assembled and color E prepared one pinwheel entry away from required color 8. The return route failed because the lower ring cell cannot move left directly: it must move up twice, then left, before ascending. That mistake exhausted the 21-step counter before the pinwheel, and no additional level was observed. I stopped at 684/700 calls; no reproduction gate was affordable and no L5 win is claimed.",
  "gotchas": [
    "L5 counter capacity is 21 actions, not L4's 42; blocked moves drain it, and the action after it reaches zero restarts or ends the game when lives are gone.",
    "The upper-left ring and lower-left ring each reset the L5 counter to 21 and disappear after collection.",
    "To reach the upper-left ring efficiently, set color only to E (two pinwheel entries), then route through the upper corridor; setting full color 8 first is one action too expensive.",
    "Upper shape pad recipe from the fresh shape: enter, exit west, re-enter to obtain [110,011,101].",
    "Lower orientation-sprite recipe observed live: with that base shape and the player at x14,y35, actions 443 produce required [101,110,011].",
    "The lower-left ring cell blocks a direct left move. Exit with up,up,left,up,up before continuing toward the upper corridor.",
    "The small top-middle green-center box was not reached; do not assume it is collectible without finding a launcher route into its apparently sealed chamber."
  ],
